## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_barkstrips.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Bark Strips builds a texture from stacked noise layers that mimic strips of tree bark. Its output works as a mask or as a base for more detailed textures, such as oak bark.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Bark Strips construit une texture de bandes d'écorce par superposition de bruits, utilisable en masque ou comme base pour une écorce de chêne.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: sets the output image size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude, Center and Mask Contrast, applied before the output range is set", "Pattern: Element Size, Offset, Tile Size as repeat period", "Strips Inflate: strip width and bulging", "Primary Edge Breakup: jagged, worn edges", "Secondary Mask and Secondary Size: visibility and scale of horizontal cuts and grooves", "Tertiary Mask and Tertiary Size: visibility and scale of vertical swirl-like cells", "Seed: randomizes the pattern while keeping the same overall look", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can be negative or above 1; use Clamp Minimum and Clamp Maximum", "Complement assumes values between 0 and 1", "Fold has no visible effect when all values are positive", "Post-processing Contrast is separate from Noise Contrast", "Non-square images should use a Tile Size matching their aspect ratio"]

